n this paper, we present an efficient, functional, and formally verified parsing algorithm for LL(1) context-free expressions based on the concept of derivatives of formal languages. Parsing with derivatives is an elegant parsing technique, which, in the general case, suffers from cubic worst-case time complexity and slow performance in practice. We specialise the parsing with derivatives algorithm to LL(1) context-free expressions, where alternatives can be chosen given a single token of lookahead. We formalise the notion of LL(1) expressions and show how to efficiently check the LL(1) property. Next, we present a novel linear-time parsing with derivatives algorithm for LL(1) expressions operating on a zipper-inspired data structure. We prove the algorithm correct in Coq and present an implementation as a part of Scallion, a parser combinators framework in Scala with enumeration and pretty printing capabilities.}\n}"}]},{"relation":"meta","args":[{"t":"entry","v":"EdelmannZippy2020"},{"t":"str","v":"container"},{"t":"str","v":"Proceedings of the 41st ACM SIGPLAN Conference on Programming Language Design and Implementation"}]},{"relation":"meta","args":[{"t":"entry","v":"EdelmannZippy2020"},{"t":"str","v":"doi"},{"t":"str","v":"10.1145/3385412.3385992"}]},{"relation":"meta","args":[{"t":"entry","v":"EdelmannZippy2020"},{"t":"str","v":"entry-type"},{"t":"str","v":"inproceedings"}]},{"relation":"meta","args":[{"t":"entry","v":"EdelmannZippy2020"},{"t":"str","v":"pages"},{"t":"str","v":"1036–1051"}]},{"relation":"meta","args":[{"t":"entry","v":"EdelmannZippy2020"},{"t":"str","v":"pldb"},{"t":"str","v":"https://pldb.kirancodes.me/p/conf/pldi/EdelmannHK20"}]},{"relation":"meta","args":[{"t":"entry","v":"EdelmannZippy2020"},{"t":"str","v":"publisher"},{"t":"str","v":"Association for Computing Machinery"}]},{"relation":"meta","args":[{"t":"entry","v":"EdelmannZippy2020"},{"t":"str","v":"url"},{"t":"str","v":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3385412.3385992"}]},{"relation":"meta","a